# Citation metadata, read by GitHub to render a "Cite this repository" button
# and by citation managers. Keep `version` in sync with pyproject.toml and
# lcsolver/__init__.py.
#
# When the JOSS paper is accepted, add a `preferred-citation:` block pointing
# at it, and add the Zenodo DOI as `doi:` below. Until then this file describes
# the software itself.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "LCsolver: An Engineering Design Interface for Pyomo"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight layer over the Pyomo modeling language for engineering design
  optimization: unit-aware model declaration, a structured interface for
  wrapping black-box analysis codes as differentiable constraints, automatic
  detection of linear, quadratic, geometric and signomial structure, and
  routing to a solver appropriate to that structure.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/codykarcher/lcsolver"
url: "https://github.com/codykarcher/lcsolver"
keywords:
  - optimization
  - engineering design
  - geometric programming
  - signomial programming
  - Pyomo
authors:
  - family-names: Karcher
    given-names: Cody J.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6062-6465"
    affiliation: "California State University, Long Beach"
  - family-names: Bynum
    given-names: Michael L.
    affiliation: "Sandia National Laboratories"
references:
